WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.890 --> 00:00:03.341
- [Mark Laita] All right. Rose

00:00:03.341 --> 00:00:04.380
- Okay.

00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:05.213
- [Mark Laita] Rose where did you grow up?

00:00:05.213 --> 00:00:06.046
Where are you from originally

00:00:06.046 --> 00:00:08.080
- [Rose] I'm born and raised
right here, Downtown LA.

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:08.913
- [Mark Laita] On Skid Row?

00:00:08.913 --> 00:00:09.746
- [Rose] On Skid Row.

00:00:09.746 --> 00:00:11.851
- [Mark Laita] Wow. And tell
me about your family then.

00:00:11.851 --> 00:00:14.080
Is it an interesting story?

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:15.920
- My mom is from Cuba,

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:17.380
My dad is from Belize

00:00:17.380 --> 00:00:19.610
but we was born and raised down here.

00:00:19.610 --> 00:00:22.430
I have six siblings, brothers and sisters.

00:00:22.430 --> 00:00:25.100
My mom had four girls and two boys.

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:27.420
My mom died when I was 16 years old.

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:30.440
My dad OD'd in front of me when I was 8.

00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:33.950
And I've never been
outside of Downtown LA.

00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:35.360
I've always been here

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:38.003
because this is the
only place that I know.

00:00:39.090 --> 00:00:42.270
I started using drugs
when I was 8 years old.

00:00:42.270 --> 00:00:44.230
And I'm 42 years old now.

00:00:44.230 --> 00:00:48.020
So I've been on it for 40,
almost 40 something years.

00:00:48.020 --> 00:00:51.869
And I just decided to get
clean like about two months ago

00:00:51.869 --> 00:00:54.100
because I feel like that's
not the life for me.

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:55.950
And I have nine kids.

00:00:55.950 --> 00:00:57.810
I have five girls and four boys,

00:00:57.810 --> 00:01:01.360
and I gave custody up to my kids dad

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:02.450
because I didn't want to put them

00:01:02.450 --> 00:01:04.280
through what I went through out here.

00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:05.840
I know what this life is like.

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:09.670
I thank God that I've
never been raped or beaten

00:01:09.670 --> 00:01:10.990
but it's because I've been homeless,

00:01:10.990 --> 00:01:12.280
I hear all the time.

00:01:12.280 --> 00:01:15.550
I live in a tent on the
next street, on Allica,

00:01:15.550 --> 00:01:17.970
and I've been homeless for 42 years.

00:01:17.970 --> 00:01:20.610
I've been taking care of my own self.

00:01:20.610 --> 00:01:22.090
At the age of 10 years old

00:01:22.090 --> 00:01:25.921
I had my own apartment by selling dope.

00:01:25.921 --> 00:01:28.230
That's all I really know
how to do is cook dope.

00:01:28.230 --> 00:01:30.232
I became the best cooker in Downtown LA.

00:01:30.232 --> 00:01:32.470
So quite naturally, everybody wanted me

00:01:32.470 --> 00:01:34.800
because a lot of people just
don't know how to make dope.

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:37.500
But now since Google's
showing you how to do it.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:41.123
But I just feel like it's
something that keeps me down here.

00:01:42.050 --> 00:01:44.980
I think that it's because I
lost my mom and dad down here

00:01:44.980 --> 00:01:47.803
and when I go anywhere else,
I don't feel them around me.

00:01:47.803 --> 00:01:48.690
- [Mark Laita] It feels like home?

00:01:48.690 --> 00:01:50.290
- Yeah. I feel like this is home.

00:01:50.290 --> 00:01:53.990
If I leave anywhere and I don't
see the downtown buildings,

00:01:53.990 --> 00:01:55.857
I get paranoid and anybody does it.

00:01:55.857 --> 00:01:57.290
You know, I'm in the car,

00:01:57.290 --> 00:01:59.364
we'd have to bring me back because

00:01:59.364 --> 00:02:01.150
these are the only streets

00:02:01.150 --> 00:02:02.153
that my mom and dad walked

00:02:02.153 --> 00:02:03.790
when I was a little girl

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:05.440
and this is the only place I know.

00:02:05.440 --> 00:02:07.860
All my brothers and sisters moved.

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:09.650
Like, all my sisters live in Bakersfield.

00:02:09.650 --> 00:02:12.030
My brothers live in Inglewood,

00:02:12.030 --> 00:02:13.850
but I choose to stay Downtown LA

00:02:13.850 --> 00:02:15.337
and I don't know why.

00:02:15.337 --> 00:02:16.260
- [Mark Laita] How about you and school?

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:17.810
- I made it to the ninth grade.

00:02:17.810 --> 00:02:19.210
I was a freshman.

00:02:19.210 --> 00:02:21.170
I had a learning disability,

00:02:21.170 --> 00:02:23.790
like, I don't read and spell good,

00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:25.883
but I'm learning.

00:02:26.840 --> 00:02:28.520
And I just remain teachable.

00:02:28.520 --> 00:02:31.600
I know every day is a
learning experience for me.

00:02:31.600 --> 00:02:33.940
And one thing I appreciate
about my mom and dad is

00:02:33.940 --> 00:02:35.490
they taught me how to take care of myself

00:02:35.490 --> 00:02:37.130
at such a young age.

00:02:37.130 --> 00:02:38.840
Due to the fact that all they done.

00:02:38.840 --> 00:02:40.510
My dad was a loan shark.

00:02:40.510 --> 00:02:43.000
My mom, all they did is do drugs.

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:44.780
So we had to learn to
take care of ourselves.

00:02:44.780 --> 00:02:46.320
We had to learn to cook for ourselves,

00:02:46.320 --> 00:02:48.827
we had to learn to take
a shower for ourselves

00:02:48.827 --> 00:02:50.610
because they was on drugs

00:02:50.610 --> 00:02:52.680
and she didn't have time to do that.

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:55.880
And that's why I choose to give my kids up

00:02:55.880 --> 00:02:57.450
because I want a better life for them.

00:02:57.450 --> 00:02:58.540
I don't want them to have to go through

00:02:58.540 --> 00:03:00.020
what I've been through.

00:03:00.020 --> 00:03:02.490
- [Mark Laita] What was your
favorite memory as a kid?

00:03:02.490 --> 00:03:04.700
- My memory as a kid is my mom and dad

00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:06.820
walking us around these streets,

00:03:06.820 --> 00:03:08.160
going up and down these streets,

00:03:08.160 --> 00:03:11.408
and that I take the same route
as when I was a little girl.

00:03:11.408 --> 00:03:15.780
And what's a coincidence,
I think it's a blessing,

00:03:15.780 --> 00:03:17.950
is my dad died in the Alexandria hotel,

00:03:17.950 --> 00:03:21.320
which is one of the most
famous hotels down here,

00:03:21.320 --> 00:03:23.910
and now that's where my mail goes.

00:03:23.910 --> 00:03:27.090
I've been back since the
age of 8 years old to now,

00:03:27.090 --> 00:03:30.170
42 years later, I'm
back in the same hotel.

00:03:30.170 --> 00:03:31.120
I'm right down the hall

00:03:31.120 --> 00:03:32.200
from where we lived when I was a kid.

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:33.410
- [Mark Laita] So you're in
a hotel or you're in a tent?

00:03:33.410 --> 00:03:35.180
- I'm out here but my friend and I

00:03:35.180 --> 00:03:37.650
take our showers and all
my mail go over there.

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:38.900
So I go over there.

00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:41.350
I'm able to go in and take a shower,

00:03:41.350 --> 00:03:42.947
warm up and come back out.

00:03:42.947 --> 00:03:43.780
- [Mark Laita] But you've
been living in a tent

00:03:43.780 --> 00:03:44.613
for how long?

00:03:44.613 --> 00:03:46.110
- I've been living in my tent for now,

00:03:46.110 --> 00:03:47.379
almost 25 years.

00:03:47.379 --> 00:03:49.170
- [Mark Laita] Can you live in a-

00:03:49.170 --> 00:03:50.003
- Yeah, I live in a tent-

00:03:50.003 --> 00:03:50.836
- [Mark Laita] No, can you live in a house

00:03:50.836 --> 00:03:53.330
or an apartment?

00:03:53.330 --> 00:03:54.880
- Yeah, if I had the-

00:03:54.880 --> 00:03:57.810
I don't receive no GR no nothing because-

00:03:57.810 --> 00:03:58.990
- [Mark Laita] So how do
you support yourself now?

00:03:58.990 --> 00:04:00.930
- Right now I just got a job

00:04:00.930 --> 00:04:03.740
working at the medical
center across the street.

00:04:03.740 --> 00:04:05.840
And that's how I've
been supporting myself.

00:04:05.840 --> 00:04:07.581
Doing that and selling drugs.

00:04:07.581 --> 00:04:09.100
- [Mark Laita] You were
selling drugs up until when,

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:10.210
just recently?

00:04:10.210 --> 00:04:11.940
- Just recently. I just
stopped two months ago

00:04:11.940 --> 00:04:13.842
when I got my job right
here across the street.

00:04:13.842 --> 00:04:14.900
- [Mark Laita] What motivated you

00:04:14.900 --> 00:04:16.260
to change your life around?

00:04:16.260 --> 00:04:17.890
- Tired of going to jail.

00:04:17.890 --> 00:04:19.130
I'm tired of going to jail.

00:04:19.130 --> 00:04:21.890
People say they got your
back, but they don't.

00:04:21.890 --> 00:04:24.310
And I realized that I was a fool

00:04:24.310 --> 00:04:27.160
because I'm out here selling
drugs for other people

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:30.180
and when I go to jail, nobody
puts money on my books.

00:04:30.180 --> 00:04:31.120
- [Mark Laita] But there's
probably something deeper

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:33.100
than tired of going to jail

00:04:33.100 --> 00:04:33.933
that's behind that.

00:04:33.933 --> 00:04:36.198
- Well you gotta be sick and
tired of being sick and tired.

00:04:36.198 --> 00:04:38.850
I know where it takes me.

00:04:38.850 --> 00:04:40.580
And I know this life.

00:04:40.580 --> 00:04:42.340
And I know that if I don't stop,

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:44.450
you see there's only two things,

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:46.543
jails, institution or death.

00:04:47.380 --> 00:04:49.660
And I don't want either one of those.

00:04:49.660 --> 00:04:51.520
I want to be something in this life.

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:54.270
I want my kids to have
something in his life.

00:04:54.270 --> 00:04:58.064
I don't want them to have
their mom die as a junkie

00:04:58.064 --> 00:04:59.990
like my mom did.

00:04:59.990 --> 00:05:02.240
- [Mark Laita] Who introduced
you to drugs at 8 years old?

00:05:02.240 --> 00:05:04.130
- All the people that I
was around, my mom and dad.

00:05:04.130 --> 00:05:05.600
I picked it up from my mom.

00:05:05.600 --> 00:05:07.420
I used to watch how they do it.

00:05:07.420 --> 00:05:09.526
And one day she put it down
and she went to the store.

00:05:09.526 --> 00:05:11.800
And when she came back, I picked it up.

00:05:11.800 --> 00:05:12.633
- [Mark Laita] That was crack?

00:05:12.633 --> 00:05:13.466
- Crack cocaine.

00:05:13.466 --> 00:05:16.940
That was back in the 80s
when it was real crack.

00:05:16.940 --> 00:05:19.110
Now I don't know what it is,

00:05:19.110 --> 00:05:20.040
but that's what made me

00:05:20.040 --> 00:05:22.340
motivate me to change my life.

00:05:22.340 --> 00:05:23.940
Because I want something better.

00:05:25.540 --> 00:05:28.610
I always like to work and have a job

00:05:28.610 --> 00:05:30.930
because I always like to have my own.

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:33.060
I don't like to get something
or to borrow something.

00:05:33.060 --> 00:05:34.140
I ask people for something

00:05:34.140 --> 00:05:37.030
and then they throw it up to your face.

00:05:37.030 --> 00:05:40.830
So I believe the best
way is to be independent

00:05:41.780 --> 00:05:43.480
and learn from my mistakes.

00:05:43.480 --> 00:05:44.723
I live and I learn.

00:05:45.620 --> 00:05:47.070
That's why I like Little Wayne's song.

00:05:47.070 --> 00:05:49.130
He say he a rookie and a vet

00:05:49.130 --> 00:05:51.180
but he still remain teachable.

00:05:51.180 --> 00:05:52.610
- [Mark Laita] Well, so what
do you think the difference is

00:05:52.610 --> 00:05:54.570
between you and everyone
else here on Skid Row,

00:05:54.570 --> 00:05:56.950
who just seems content
to stay here forever?

00:05:56.950 --> 00:05:58.940
- My thing, I think the difference is,

00:05:58.940 --> 00:06:01.400
is everybody have choices

00:06:01.400 --> 00:06:02.233
and it's up to us

00:06:02.233 --> 00:06:05.380
what we make and what we want.

00:06:05.380 --> 00:06:07.730
I believe that they struggling
the fence right now.

00:06:07.730 --> 00:06:09.993
They battling with good and evil.

00:06:10.850 --> 00:06:14.200
And the devil is powerful,

00:06:14.200 --> 00:06:15.890
like Jesus is powerful,

00:06:15.890 --> 00:06:17.453
but only if we let them win.

00:06:18.490 --> 00:06:19.916
And if you want to do better,

00:06:19.916 --> 00:06:22.340
you're going to do better.

00:06:22.340 --> 00:06:23.898
I think what keeps them down here

00:06:23.898 --> 00:06:26.750
is that they lose their
morals and their values.

00:06:26.750 --> 00:06:29.570
They forget the way their
parents raised them.

00:06:29.570 --> 00:06:31.320
They lose all home bases.

00:06:31.320 --> 00:06:32.238
And when they come out here

00:06:32.238 --> 00:06:36.030
they get adapted to the new
rules, the street rules,

00:06:36.030 --> 00:06:37.400
which is the wrong rules,

00:06:37.400 --> 00:06:39.140
'cause the streets don't love nobody.

00:06:39.140 --> 00:06:39.973
- [Mark Laita] Yeah, but the street life

00:06:39.973 --> 00:06:40.820
seems to be very addictive

00:06:40.820 --> 00:06:41.653
for a lot of people.

00:06:41.653 --> 00:06:44.370
- It's very addictive because of the drugs

00:06:44.370 --> 00:06:47.340
and the weak souls that's out here.

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:49.770
Because it's very powerful,

00:06:49.770 --> 00:06:51.440
but we all have a choice too.

00:06:51.440 --> 00:06:53.510
What we want to make with our lives.

00:06:53.510 --> 00:06:54.450
Sometimes you got to go.

00:06:54.450 --> 00:06:56.450
Some people gotta hit rock bottom.

00:06:56.450 --> 00:06:59.800
And some people just know
when it's time to let it go.

00:06:59.800 --> 00:07:01.510
And me, I want to live.

00:07:01.510 --> 00:07:04.780
And to live down here, I
have to be clean and sober.

00:07:04.780 --> 00:07:06.100
If not, I'm going to be walking around

00:07:06.100 --> 00:07:07.040
like these crazy women.

00:07:07.040 --> 00:07:09.030
Bare feeted, with no clothes on

00:07:09.030 --> 00:07:11.560
running up and down the
street, talking to myself.

00:07:11.560 --> 00:07:14.550
And I always pray to God
that I never be like that.

00:07:14.550 --> 00:07:16.518
And I thank God that I haven't yet.

00:07:16.518 --> 00:07:19.453
- [Mark Laita] What's
been your lowest point?

00:07:20.900 --> 00:07:25.590
- Me choosing this life, the
Skid Row life over my kids.

00:07:25.590 --> 00:07:26.523
That's my lowest.

00:07:27.618 --> 00:07:30.200
I was willing to give my kids up

00:07:30.200 --> 00:07:32.750
so that I can be out here on drugs.

00:07:32.750 --> 00:07:34.378
That's the lowest.

00:07:34.378 --> 00:07:35.211
- [Mark Laita] What do you think

00:07:35.211 --> 00:07:36.044
most people that don't do drugs

00:07:36.044 --> 00:07:38.283
don't understand about addiction?

00:07:39.700 --> 00:07:42.417
- It is where it could
take you and the things-

00:07:42.417 --> 00:07:44.270
- [Mark Laita] But it's
not a conscious choice

00:07:44.270 --> 00:07:45.170
these people make.

00:07:46.120 --> 00:07:48.773
- No, it's something that's happened.

00:07:51.372 --> 00:07:53.070
It's like having a
gorilla on your shoulder

00:07:53.070 --> 00:07:54.549
and you're fighting him

00:07:54.549 --> 00:07:56.163
but he's holding on.

00:07:57.780 --> 00:07:58.880
That's what it's like.

00:08:00.570 --> 00:08:01.706
It's hard.

00:08:01.706 --> 00:08:02.719
- [Mark Laita] Do you have friends.

00:08:02.719 --> 00:08:03.552
- No.

00:08:04.519 --> 00:08:05.729
- [Mark Laita] Have you ever had friends?

00:08:05.729 --> 00:08:07.010
- No.

00:08:07.010 --> 00:08:08.970
- I don't believe in friends.

00:08:08.970 --> 00:08:10.900
Friends is backstabbers.

00:08:10.900 --> 00:08:12.840
The only friends is my family.

00:08:12.840 --> 00:08:14.390
That's the only friends I need.

00:08:15.290 --> 00:08:16.753
And my kids.

00:08:16.753 --> 00:08:18.710
- [Mark Laita] You ever been in love?

00:08:18.710 --> 00:08:20.630
- In love? Yeah.

00:08:20.630 --> 00:08:22.680
I was with my kids dad for 28 years.

00:08:22.680 --> 00:08:25.610
9 kids by the same man.

00:08:25.610 --> 00:08:27.530
And I went to prison for selling drugs.

00:08:27.530 --> 00:08:29.960
When I got out, he cheated on me.

00:08:29.960 --> 00:08:32.330
And that's why I been out here ever since.

00:08:32.330 --> 00:08:35.080
I just choose to do my own thing.

00:08:35.080 --> 00:08:37.430
But I choose not to let
nobody get close to me.

00:08:39.842 --> 00:08:41.740
'Cause the flesh was made for sins

00:08:42.610 --> 00:08:44.800
and I have trust issues

00:08:44.800 --> 00:08:47.600
because I give people
the benefit of the doubt.

00:08:47.600 --> 00:08:48.970
And just what I think they're gonna to do

00:08:48.970 --> 00:08:49.900
is what they try to do.

00:08:49.900 --> 00:08:51.840
But I already be prepared for it.

00:08:51.840 --> 00:08:53.320
So I believe if you stay ready,

00:08:53.320 --> 00:08:54.720
you don't have to get ready.

00:08:57.170 --> 00:08:58.160
- [Mark Laita] What's
the most important lesson

00:08:58.160 --> 00:09:00.410
you've learned in all your years out here?

00:09:00.410 --> 00:09:02.120
- [Rose] How to not do nothing to others

00:09:02.120 --> 00:09:03.633
that I don't want done to me.

00:09:04.620 --> 00:09:06.720
Treat people the way I want to be treated.

00:09:08.220 --> 00:09:10.580
It's like the concept, empathy.

00:09:10.580 --> 00:09:13.350
The ability to imagine how others feel.

00:09:13.350 --> 00:09:16.280
And in order to progress
your empathetic skills,

00:09:16.280 --> 00:09:17.187
you must ask yourself,

00:09:17.187 --> 00:09:20.690
"How would you feel under
the same circumstances?"

00:09:20.690 --> 00:09:21.737
That's what I think.

00:09:21.737 --> 00:09:22.880
- [Mark Laita] So with
all your time down here

00:09:22.880 --> 00:09:24.167
living on the streets,

00:09:24.167 --> 00:09:26.640
what qualities do you
think you've developed

00:09:26.640 --> 00:09:28.720
that most people don't have.

00:09:28.720 --> 00:09:30.210
The street life is very different.

00:09:30.210 --> 00:09:32.170
- [Rose] How to love myself.

00:09:32.170 --> 00:09:34.470
That I can't love others,
unless I love myself

00:09:35.870 --> 00:09:39.530
because I can tell everybody
I love you, but do I love me?

00:09:39.530 --> 00:09:40.490
If I don't love me?

00:09:40.490 --> 00:09:42.063
How can I love someone else.

00:09:43.020 --> 00:09:44.823
And how to be loyal.

00:09:45.750 --> 00:09:48.530
Because I don't do nothing
to them, but they do to me.

00:09:48.530 --> 00:09:50.850
And they have done a lot of things to me,

00:09:50.850 --> 00:09:53.230
and what I do, I pray for them.

00:09:53.230 --> 00:09:56.220
And I asked God to help
them and to forgive them

00:09:56.220 --> 00:09:58.320
because they know not what they do.

00:09:58.320 --> 00:10:01.366
- [Mark Laita] What has
helped you gain the ability

00:10:01.366 --> 00:10:03.374
to love yourself

00:10:03.374 --> 00:10:08.374
- To me is being able to accept my world.

00:10:08.620 --> 00:10:11.093
Being able to realize
that I'm my worst enemy.

00:10:12.130 --> 00:10:13.610
That no one could do nothing to me,

00:10:13.610 --> 00:10:14.963
unless I allow them to.

00:10:15.960 --> 00:10:18.250
To be able to wake up and make a choice.

00:10:18.250 --> 00:10:20.345
Am I just gonna sit on
the ground and be a bum

00:10:20.345 --> 00:10:22.980
or am I gonna go out and look for a job?

00:10:22.980 --> 00:10:23.970
Am I just going to sit here

00:10:23.970 --> 00:10:25.220
and get drunk and get high

00:10:25.220 --> 00:10:27.900
and say, poor me, poor me

00:10:27.900 --> 00:10:29.570
or am I going to do
something about my life

00:10:29.570 --> 00:10:31.018
to make it better?

00:10:31.018 --> 00:10:32.523
That's what I believe it is.

00:10:36.228 --> 00:10:37.061
- [Mark Laita] Can you imagine

00:10:37.061 --> 00:10:37.894
what your life would have been like

00:10:37.894 --> 00:10:40.410
if you had two parents that raised you

00:10:40.410 --> 00:10:41.420
and stuck together and didn't-

00:10:41.420 --> 00:10:43.870
- Yeah, I probably wouldn't
have never did drugs.

00:10:45.809 --> 00:10:47.660
Well, I really don't regret it

00:10:47.660 --> 00:10:49.120
because I learned from all of it.

00:10:49.120 --> 00:10:51.650
The only thing I just miss my mom and dad

00:10:51.650 --> 00:10:53.180
but I know they my guardian angels

00:10:53.180 --> 00:10:54.240
and they with me

00:10:55.540 --> 00:10:58.110
and that they would want
to see me doing better

00:10:58.110 --> 00:11:00.030
than what I've been doing.

00:11:00.030 --> 00:11:02.390
- [Rose] And so that's my goal.

00:11:02.390 --> 00:11:06.593
Is to do better for
myself and for my kids.

00:11:07.690 --> 00:11:08.523
- [Mark Laita] All right Rose.

00:11:08.523 --> 00:11:09.764
Thank you so much for sharing your story.

00:11:09.764 --> 00:11:10.597
- Thank you so much.

00:11:10.597 --> 00:11:11.600
- [Mark Laita] I wish
you the best of luck.

00:11:11.600 --> 00:11:13.203
Thank you. God bless you.

00:11:17.950 --> 00:11:19.690
- [Rose] So what do you think?

00:11:19.690 --> 00:11:20.900
- [Mark Laita] Finally a positive story.

00:11:20.900 --> 00:11:22.970
- [Rose] I know you got it.

00:11:22.970 --> 00:11:24.920
- [Mark Laita] I got so many dark ones.

